  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-326539",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find an amount that's $25%$ *less than* $$64,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%-25%=75%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n75%=\\frac{75}{100}=0.75\n$$\n\nSo, to find $75%$ of $$64,$ we multiply $$64$ by $0.75:$\n\n$$\n0.75\\cdot $64=$48\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sale price of the table is $$48.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
